[32m+[m[32m# Linux System Health Monitor[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mA Bash-based Linux system monitoring tool developed as part of my DevOps learning project.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Overview[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThis project provides a lightweight system health check for Linux environments.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mIt monitors:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- CPU load average normalized by logical CPU count[m
[32m+[m[32m- Memory utilization[m
[32m+[m[32m- Root filesystem disk usage[m
[32m+[m[32m- Presence of a specified process[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe script prints a status report and returns a nonzero exit code when a warning is detected.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Requirements[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Linux[m
[32m+[m[32m- Bash[m
[32m+[m[32m- GNU coreutils[m
[32m+[m[32m- awk[m
[32m+[m[32m- procps utilities (`free`, `pgrep`, `nproc`)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Usage[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mFrom the repository root:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32m./week02/scripts/health-check.sh[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mTo check a particular process:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32m./week02/scripts/health-check.sh sshd[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Configuration[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThe script currently uses these thresholds:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m| Metric | Warning threshold |[m
[32m+[m[32m|---|---|[m
[32m+[m[32m| Normalized CPU load | Greater than 1.0 |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Memory usage | Greater than 80% |[m
[32m+[m[32m| Disk usage | Greater than 85% |[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mThresholds are configured in the script.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Exit Codes[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- `0`: All checks passed[m
[32m+[m[32m- `1`: One or more checks reported a warning[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Testing[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mRun:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```bash[m
[32m+[m[32mbash -n week02/scripts/health-check.sh[m
[32m+[m[32mshellcheck week02/scripts/health-check.sh[m
[32m+[m[32m./week02/scripts/test-health-check.sh[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Limitations[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- CPU load average is not the same as instantaneous CPU utilization.[m
[32m+[m[32m- The script checks only the root filesystem.[m
[32m+[m[32m- Process detection is based on process names.[m
[32m+[m[32m- The monitor is intended as a learning project, not a replacement for a production observability platform.[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Future Improvements[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- Configurable thresholds via command-line arguments[m
[32m+[m[32m- More comprehensive automated tests[m
[32m+[m[32m- Monitoring multiple filesystems[m
[32m+[m[32m- JSON output for integration with other tools[m
[32m+[m[32m- CI/CD integration using GitHub Actions[m
[32m+[m
